The cell 'span verbatim in the document / value the whole of the span' specifies that the span is exactly present in the document and the value is identical to the span. For the kernel `conformance.kernel.grounding`, the rule states it provides the grounding verdict with "no relaxation, value-in-span checked" [cf3ead255ba521d3]. In the input, the span "The sun is hot" is verbatim in the document and the value "The sun is hot" is the whole of the span; the rule implies a verdict of GROUNDED. In the rewritten text, I change the value to "The sun is cold", which is no longer inside the span. The rule then implies a verdict of VALUE_NOT_IN_SPAN. Thus, the verdict moves.